<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25562" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάπλοος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά-πλους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			Adj., <i>sailing across</i> or <i>sailing continually,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. καθίστασαν λεών</span> they kept them
				<i>at the oar,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				382
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάπλους</span></b> , ὁ, <i>a voyage across,
				passage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὸ Κήναιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.93
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ τῆς οἰκείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>room for sailing through, passage,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυοῖν νεοῖν</span> for two ships abreast,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				4.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>cross-channel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Criti.</u>
				118e
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>